/bazel-*

# If $LEETCODE_STORAGE_HOME points directly at this checkout (rather than a
# copy elsewhere), leetcode.nvim/harness.lua write real per-problem files
# here. This repo is a generic module library -- personal solve progress
# doesn't belong in it. Real LeetCode frontend ids start at 1; the tracked
# demo deliberately uses id 0 (see README.md), so this pattern only ever
# ignores real solves, never the demo. BUILD.bazel is NOT ignored: real
# usage still edits it, but as a visible diff you'd have to consciously
# `git add`, not a silently-untracked file.
/solutions/[1-9]*
